WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.740
In this video, you add an openSUSE Leap cloud image to SUSE Virtualization from a download URL. Virtual machines boot from images like this one.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.190
On the Images page, select Create.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.760
Choose the namespace for the image.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.990
Give the image a name.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:26.680
Keep URL as the source. The cluster downloads the file itself, so nothing passes through your browser.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:32.880
Paste the download address of the openSUSE Leap sixteen minimal cloud image.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.400
The Storage tab shows the storage class for the image. Keep the default.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.860
Virtual machine disks created from this image use the same storage class.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:49.110
Select Create.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:58.130
The download finishes and the progress column shows Completed. The image is ready for new virtual machines.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:04.931
The image is ready. Next, you add an SSH key so you can log in to your virtual machines.
